perl's rule (gv.c, S_gv_magicalize / the `global' names): an unqualified identifier in ENV INC ARGV ARGVOUT SIG STDIN STDOUT STDERR (and the punctuation / ^X names) always refers to main::.  The same rule should hold for the variables (`package Q; our @INC` is @main::INC).  LOW: real code qualifies hook methods (`sub Foo::INC`) because perl forces it.  Probe: s531a scratch/s531a/pr/specname.pl.
